  "question": "If $\\tan^{-1}\\frac{x-5}{x-6} + \\tan^{-1}\\frac{x+5}{x+6} = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$, find $x$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "Use identity $\\tan^{-1}A+\\tan^{-1}B=\\tan^{-1}\\frac{A+B}{1-AB}$.<br /><br />After simplification we obtain:<br /><br />$\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{60-2x^2}{11}\\right)=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$.<br /><br />Hence $\\frac{60-2x^2}{11}=1$.<br /><br />Thus $60-2x^2=11$.<br /><br />$2x^2=49$.<br /><br />$x^2=\\frac{49}{2}$.<br /><br />Therefore $x=\\pm\\frac{7}{\\sqrt2}$.",
  "explanation_image": [],
